@Library.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5006

### The ids below are the ones the Development seed produces on a fresh database.
### Books:     1 Dune, 2 Neuromancer, 3 Snow Crash, 5 Foundation, 7 Hyperion, 10 A Fire Upon the Deep
### Borrowers: 1 Alice, 2 Bob, 3 Clara, 4 Daniel, 5 Eve (nothing returned yet), 6 Frank (no loans)

### Inventory: what are the most borrowed books?
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/books/most-borrowed?limit=5
Accept: application/json

### The same question restricted to the seeded window. Five seeded loans start before it and drop out.
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/books/most-borrowed?limit=5&from=2026-08-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-08-31T00:00:00Z
Accept: application/json

### Rejected before it reaches the service: limit is capped at 100. Expect 400.
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/books/most-borrowed?limit=1000
Accept: application/json

### User activity: who borrowed the most in the seeded window?
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/borrowers/top?limit=5&from=2026-08-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-08-31T00:00:00Z
Accept: application/json

### Reading pace for Alice: 412 pages over 7 days plus 204 over a same-day loan, so 616 / 8 = 77 pages a day.
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/borrowers/1/reading-pace
Accept: application/json

### Eve has only an open loan, so there is nothing to measure: averagePagesPerDay is null.
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/borrowers/5/reading-pace
Accept: application/json

### An id nobody has. Expect 404.
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/borrowers/999999/reading-pace
Accept: application/json

### Borrowing patterns: what else did Dune's readers take out?
GET {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/books/1/also-borrowed?limit=5
Accept: application/json

### Lending: borrow a book. Expect 201 and a loan id.
POST {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "borrowerId": 6,
  "bookId": 10
}

### Hyperion has a single copy and Alice still has it out. Expect 409 — the book exists,
### it is the state that conflicts.
POST {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "borrowerId": 6,
  "bookId": 7
}

### A book that does not exist. Expect 404 rather than 409.
POST {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "borrowerId": 6,
  "bookId": 999999
}

### Return the loan created above — replace 20 with the loanId that came back.
POST {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/loans/20/return

### Call it again. Still 200, now with "alreadyReturned": true and the original date.
POST {{Library.Api_HostAddress}}/api/loans/20/return
